# Environment Variables — Backend

Copy this file to `backend/.env` and fill in your values.
Never commit the `.env` file — it is in `.gitignore`.

```bash
# MongoDB Connection URI
# Default: local MongoDB instance
# For cloud: use your MongoDB Atlas connection string
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/gridpulse

# JWT Signing Secret
# IMPORTANT: Change this to a long, random string in production
# Generate one with: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(64).toString('hex'))"
JWT_SECRET=gridpulse-secret-key-change-in-production-use-64-char-random-string

# Express server port
PORT=5001
```

## Notes

- `MONGODB_URI` is optional — the app runs with an in-memory store if MongoDB is unavailable
- `JWT_SECRET` defaults to a demo value if not set — always override in any deployed environment
- `PORT` defaults to 5001 if not set
